    {
      "id": 226063,
      "name": "Dr. Kaylo Epsilon",
      "username": "Dr_Kaylo_Epsilon",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dr_kaylo_epsilon/{size}/2024_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-03-21T18:44:29.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"monogarden\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/0ea827/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> monogarden:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I tend to not pay any attention to the card backs since I only play digitally and it never occurred to me that you’d be able to see what deck it was from.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Also relevant in digital when you’re in the Temple of Zhu Long, except there it’s the cards atop your hero decks that you might want to be aware of.</p>\n<p>Especially if you’ve done something that shuffled a Shinobi Assassin out from the top of your deck and into the middle, so can’t rely on the simple “Next time I draw a card, NINJAS!” heuristic.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:59:51.084Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
